17592186049823 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-552d2b63-c89f-57b7-ada2-5c8de2617c52" "step-4c3177ec-d11e-5af5-a30f-64f33bad6ce6" "step-49ba4a41-efbb-530f-82bb-ce4e6b9af5f6"] :activity/first-step "step-552d2b63-c89f-57b7-ada2-5c8de2617c52" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-552d2b63-c89f-57b7-ada2-5c8de2617c52" :step/id #uuid "552d2b63-c89f-57b7-ada2-5c8de2617c52" :step/content "question-1615e308-0f55-5459-8614-e5b1b28bfe28" :step/next "step-4c3177ec-d11e-5af5-a30f-64f33bad6ce6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4c3177ec-d11e-5af5-a30f-64f33bad6ce6" :step/id #uuid "4c3177ec-d11e-5af5-a30f-64f33bad6ce6" :step/content "question-4853c7f3-55af-53da-b6a8-b7e1a0edc0bd" :step/next "step-49ba4a41-efbb-530f-82bb-ce4e6b9af5f6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-49ba4a41-efbb-530f-82bb-ce4e6b9af5f6" :step/id #uuid "49ba4a41-efbb-530f-82bb-ce4e6b9af5f6" :step/content "question-18e9c87c-d5d7-52d0-922d-e65af5fe041b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186062401 :answer-field/choices 17592186062402] [:db/retract 17592186062401 :answer-field/choices 17592186062403] [:db/retract 17592186062401 :answer-field/choices 17592186062404] [:db/retract 17592186062401 :answer-field/choices 17592186062405] [:db/retract 17592186062401 :answer-field/choices 17592186062406] {:db/id 17592186064376 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e4e15d3e-925b-56d4-bf57-253dd32acaf7" "question-a02e865a-6a6d-5b10-8171-4b544dbd46b3" "question-f3d27d1e-a375-5722-8f78-27b79ebf66c3" "question-7b7d80eb-f47e-553b-8d7c-69b51e01b399" "question-b06ab3d9-3b8c-5c9f-a694-75f899defb02"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064377 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-38e9b5c8-f7c2-5d27-9b07-5dff34e427b9" "question-1c009d1d-9f23-53f4-ac53-e3aab6d30ee8" "question-6798c7d5-6dc4-50ce-934a-27d8986f8abb" "question-4e4521f6-9e6d-5c0e-807a-ed8494a208e7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064378 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2d8efcf9-a827-5e33-8982-8c950b1390fe" "question-94a70c07-52ed-54e0-b434-f6f0663ba853" "question-dd9599f1-ed67-5948-967c-4c445ad154d3" "question-68f6bf29-8273-5b7e-a834-752eee067f78"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e4e15d3e-925b-56d4-bf57-253dd32acaf7" :question/id #uuid "e4e15d3e-925b-56d4-bf57-253dd32acaf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343194" :question/problem "![](images/99/996768e4b1ce8ae57bcf3cce61059f8349c307ea9f05c9c1f51831ff6fd8ae68.png)\n\nA rectangular loaf of rising bread dough is squeezed between two rigid side panels that keep its width fixed. The length of the loaf is decreasing by $20\\,\\text{mm}\\text{/s},$ while the $60\\,\\text{mm}$ width does not change. If the volume of the loaf is constant, how fast is its height changing when its dimensions are $100\\,\\text{mm}$ in length and $30\\,\\text{mm}$ in height?\n\nThe height is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =100\\,\\text{mm}, \\\\ y & =60\\,\\text{mm}, \\\\ z & =30\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-20\\,\\text{mm}\\text{/s}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =0\\,{\\text{mm}}^{3}\\text{/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=100\\,\\text{mm},$ $y=60\\,\\text{mm}$ and $z=30\\,\\text{mm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSince $y$ is not changing and $y=60,$ we get\n\n$$\nV=60xz.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(60xz) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =60x(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+60z(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =60(100)(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+60(30)(-20) \\\\ 0 & =6000(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})-36\\,000 \\\\ 36\\,000 & =6000(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =6\\,\\text{mm}\\text{/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the height of the solid is increasing at a rate of $6\\,\\text{mm}/\\text{s}$ at the moment when $x=100\\,\\text{mm},$ $y=60\\,\\text{mm}$ and $z=30\\,\\text{mm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b852a09c-ea6b-5010-b9b3-a3b637cbd328"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b852a09c-ea6b-5010-b9b3-a3b637cbd328" :answer-field/id #uuid "b852a09c-ea6b-5010-b9b3-a3b637cbd328" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f9e53027-3a83-5961-948b-e0b5df7093f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f9e53027-3a83-5961-948b-e0b5df7093f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9e53027-3a83-5961-948b-e0b5df7093f8" :answer/id #uuid "f9e53027-3a83-5961-948b-e0b5df7093f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a02e865a-6a6d-5b10-8171-4b544dbd46b3" :question/id #uuid "a02e865a-6a6d-5b10-8171-4b544dbd46b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-2795" :question/problem "![](images/52/52448daf1f9aea06b4ab4713756080ddb3ab465b4fae8f92b65a54c251a81d5e.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing by $8\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}$ and its height increasing at a rate of $1\\,\\text{cm/min}.$ If the volume of the rectangular prism is decreasing at a rate of $50\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min},$  how fast is its width changing when its dimensions are $10\\,\\text{cm}$ in length, $15\\,\\text{cm}$ in width and $5\\,\\text{cm}$ in height?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ y & =5\\text{ cm}, \\\\ z & =15\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-8\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-50{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=10\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=5\\,\\text{cm},$ and $z=15\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x\\cdot y\\cdot z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =xy(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+xz(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+yz(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-50 & =(10)(5)(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+(10)(15)(1)+(15)(5)(-8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =8\\text{ cm}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the solid is increasing at a rate of $8\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=10\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=5\\,\\text{cm},$ and $z=15\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f60c8b13-b572-54f8-b997-4b367f683cdf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f60c8b13-b572-54f8-b997-4b367f683cdf" :answer-field/id #uuid "f60c8b13-b572-54f8-b997-4b367f683cdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-31598524-9782-5a60-9550-6527d0e8e332" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7fd5b608-b1ff-5a9d-9abd-12c753eba961" "answer-d37f3eb9-f956-5d80-bd59-824978a5c588" "answer-1f044fe5-a78a-503c-8136-573bff49033a" "answer-31598524-9782-5a60-9550-6527d0e8e332" "answer-2903205c-6d62-59f7-9321-c5aced82f76b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7fd5b608-b1ff-5a9d-9abd-12c753eba961" :answer/id #uuid "7fd5b608-b1ff-5a9d-9abd-12c753eba961" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d37f3eb9-f956-5d80-bd59-824978a5c588" :answer/id #uuid "d37f3eb9-f956-5d80-bd59-824978a5c588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f044fe5-a78a-503c-8136-573bff49033a" :answer/id #uuid "1f044fe5-a78a-503c-8136-573bff49033a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31598524-9782-5a60-9550-6527d0e8e332" :answer/id #uuid "31598524-9782-5a60-9550-6527d0e8e332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2903205c-6d62-59f7-9321-c5aced82f76b" :answer/id #uuid "2903205c-6d62-59f7-9321-c5aced82f76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3d27d1e-a375-5722-8f78-27b79ebf66c3" :question/id #uuid "f3d27d1e-a375-5722-8f78-27b79ebf66c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-343180" :question/problem "![](images/49/4946691a4258fb310ec7052f1edd5a1b9117ca7daeea152e4a1b01b11a624e2e.png)\n\nJennie fills an aquarium, in the shape of a rectangular prism that is $50\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $25\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, with water from a tap. What is the rate of change of the water level if the volume is increasing at a rate of $250\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{h}?$\n\nThe water level is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{h}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =50\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ y & =25\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=250\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{h}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=50\\,\\text{cm}$ and $y=25\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nV=(50)(25)z=1250z.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1250z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =1250(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known value into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}250 & =1250(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =0.2\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water level is increasing at a rate of $0.2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-41fb01ad-fc9d-5c1d-96c5-0e78cb67f17e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41fb01ad-fc9d-5c1d-96c5-0e78cb67f17e" :answer-field/id #uuid "41fb01ad-fc9d-5c1d-96c5-0e78cb67f17e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-442e3b6f-0334-59dc-bbe2-9c521ab09118" :answer-field/choices ["answer-442e3b6f-0334-59dc-bbe2-9c521ab09118"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-442e3b6f-0334-59dc-bbe2-9c521ab09118" :answer/id #uuid "442e3b6f-0334-59dc-bbe2-9c521ab09118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b7d80eb-f47e-553b-8d7c-69b51e01b399" :question/id #uuid "7b7d80eb-f47e-553b-8d7c-69b51e01b399" :question/math-academy-id "q-116080" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e11ec3379c969bbc8499f36978f3a39efe1342ee6563569949dbcb61611ab5f4.png)\n\nA cube of ice is melting uniformly at a rate of $204\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min},$ where $x$ is the length of its edge. How fast is each edge of the ice block decreasing when the volume of the cube is $216\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $V$ be the volume of the ice cube. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-204\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ when $V=216\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$\n\n  We start with the formula for the volume of the cube:\n  \n\n$$\nV={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBefore we plug in the known values, we need to find the value of $x$ when $V=216\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={x}^{3} \\\\ 216 & ={x}^{3} \\\\ x & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug $x=6$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-204$ into the expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ -204 & =3(6)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{17}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sides of the cube are decreasing at a rate of $\\frac{17}{9}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=6\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f8097c0f-208a-5485-aa29-effca04536fd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f8097c0f-208a-5485-aa29-effca04536fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8097c0f-208a-5485-aa29-effca04536fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c8f1f4a6-e404-5f43-830e-76e2bf630422" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6e27c78-c668-58d3-9f71-075b75e4b8fd" "answer-57e11df3-0c32-5640-afed-b16fcbb6e9cb" "answer-027d65cd-408d-54f0-8851-920431c6df14" "answer-c8f1f4a6-e404-5f43-830e-76e2bf630422" "answer-3f077957-2111-50ad-b8a3-980fad8a395e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6e27c78-c668-58d3-9f71-075b75e4b8fd" :answer/id #uuid "f6e27c78-c668-58d3-9f71-075b75e4b8fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57e11df3-0c32-5640-afed-b16fcbb6e9cb" :answer/id #uuid "57e11df3-0c32-5640-afed-b16fcbb6e9cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027d65cd-408d-54f0-8851-920431c6df14" :answer/id #uuid "027d65cd-408d-54f0-8851-920431c6df14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{6}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f1f4a6-e404-5f43-830e-76e2bf630422" :answer/id #uuid "c8f1f4a6-e404-5f43-830e-76e2bf630422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{9}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f077957-2111-50ad-b8a3-980fad8a395e" :answer/id #uuid "3f077957-2111-50ad-b8a3-980fad8a395e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{17}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b06ab3d9-3b8c-5c9f-a694-75f899defb02" :question/id #uuid "b06ab3d9-3b8c-5c9f-a694-75f899defb02" :question/math-academy-id "q-314513" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b45121fc7e3b6de3e37053b944bed610e55d337b7c73d89b258a89f903ad0c2.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing by $1.5\\text{ feet}\\text{/min}$ and its height is increasing at a rate of $1\\text{ feet/min}.$ If the volume of the rectangular prism is decreasing at a rate of $9{\\text{ feet}}^{3}\\text{/min},$ how fast is its width decreasing when its dimensions are $5\\,\\text{feet}$ in length, $3\\,\\text{feet}$ in width, and $2\\,\\text{feet}$ in height? Assume that the rate of decrease of width is positive.\n\nThe width is decreasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{feet}/\\text{min}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\,\\text{feet}, \\\\ y & =3\\,\\text{feet}, \\\\ z & =2\\,\\text{feet}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-1.5\\,\\text{feet}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\,\\text{feet}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-9\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=5\\,\\text{feet},$ $y=3\\,\\text{feet},$ and $z=2\\,\\text{feet}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x\\cdot y\\cdot z) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =xy(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+xz(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+yz(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9 & =(5)(3)(1)+(5)(2)(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+(2)(3)(-1.5) \\\\ -9 & =15+10\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})-9 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the solid is decreasing at a rate of $1.5\\,\\text{feet}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=5\\,\\text{feet},$ $y=2\\,\\text{feet},$ and $z=3\\,\\text{feet}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4367237c-774c-57e1-b55c-8026f7a5b4ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4367237c-774c-57e1-b55c-8026f7a5b4ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "4367237c-774c-57e1-b55c-8026f7a5b4ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eb50cfa7-d5fd-5e1c-bd95-f2d2d5a2cd71" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb50cfa7-d5fd-5e1c-bd95-f2d2d5a2cd71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb50cfa7-d5fd-5e1c-bd95-f2d2d5a2cd71" :answer/id #uuid "eb50cfa7-d5fd-5e1c-bd95-f2d2d5a2cd71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-38e9b5c8-f7c2-5d27-9b07-5dff34e427b9" :question/id #uuid "38e9b5c8-f7c2-5d27-9b07-5dff34e427b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-116519" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7aad5aea708422b331b19ab2e9c7586b5b037054347841530db829e2fc3c9075.png)\n\nIf the surface area of a cube is increasing at a rate of $144{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\text{/s},$ at what rate are the edges changing when each edge is $4\\text{ cm}?$ Assume that each edge is increasing at the same rate." :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the side of the cube, let $S$ be its surface area, and let $V$ be its volume. All of the variables change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=144\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=4\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $x$ knowing the rate of change of $S.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the cube:\n\n$$\nS=6{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(S) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 144 & =12(4)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the edges are changing at a rate of $3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2eb92cf-2f1b-5649-bd7d-f3661cb6b3bd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2eb92cf-2f1b-5649-bd7d-f3661cb6b3bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2eb92cf-2f1b-5649-bd7d-f3661cb6b3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-757d12dc-4e03-5cbe-aa1a-74dced4f3122" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3538c791-2780-512a-91df-ad5c36e93cd6" "answer-757d12dc-4e03-5cbe-aa1a-74dced4f3122" "answer-5013e2ef-3020-5d40-a3be-1725d68decf3" "answer-46d896d9-f073-535d-b7d9-9558f591b993" "answer-2d9da049-a5de-5ea0-9fe8-5b987a55d80e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3538c791-2780-512a-91df-ad5c36e93cd6" :answer/id #uuid "3538c791-2780-512a-91df-ad5c36e93cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-757d12dc-4e03-5cbe-aa1a-74dced4f3122" :answer/id #uuid "757d12dc-4e03-5cbe-aa1a-74dced4f3122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5013e2ef-3020-5d40-a3be-1725d68decf3" :answer/id #uuid "5013e2ef-3020-5d40-a3be-1725d68decf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46d896d9-f073-535d-b7d9-9558f591b993" :answer/id #uuid "46d896d9-f073-535d-b7d9-9558f591b993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d9da049-a5de-5ea0-9fe8-5b987a55d80e" :answer/id #uuid "2d9da049-a5de-5ea0-9fe8-5b987a55d80e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c009d1d-9f23-53f4-ac53-e3aab6d30ee8" :question/id #uuid "1c009d1d-9f23-53f4-ac53-e3aab6d30ee8" :question/math-academy-id "q-343214" :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c11298d151c2f93fbe7d00352386ff859f788ced2641ebe724fd7ddd9f7d205.png)\n\nA cube-shaped inflatable toy is being filled so that its surface area is growing at a rate of $150\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.$ How fast is its edge increasing when each edge is $5\\text{ in}?$\n\nThe cube's edge is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{in}/\\text{min}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the side of the cube, let $S$ be its surface area, and let $V$ be its volume. All of the variables change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=150\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=5\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $x$ knowing the rate of change of $S.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the cube:\n\n$$\nS=6{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(S) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 150 & =12(5)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the edges are increasing at a rate of $2.5\\,\\text{in}/\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6d9c5f0-1b59-5800-900a-7031812188d1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6d9c5f0-1b59-5800-900a-7031812188d1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6d9c5f0-1b59-5800-900a-7031812188d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7e1973b6-3fd1-50a3-a8c8-08ed11168d56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e1973b6-3fd1-50a3-a8c8-08ed11168d56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e1973b6-3fd1-50a3-a8c8-08ed11168d56" :answer/id #uuid "7e1973b6-3fd1-50a3-a8c8-08ed11168d56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6798c7d5-6dc4-50ce-934a-27d8986f8abb" :question/id #uuid "6798c7d5-6dc4-50ce-934a-27d8986f8abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-116498" :question/problem "![](images/32/324e3b2752fd398e47ce066dfc44f8a4d96cc3d7916f917fa142485ae86bf48f.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing at a rate of $5\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min},$ the width is increasing at a rate of $11\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min},$ and the height is decreasing at a rate of $5\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}.$ How fast is the surface area increasing when the dimensions of the rectangular prism are $2\\,\\text{cm}$ in length, $4\\,\\text{cm}$ in width and $7\\,\\text{cm}$ in height?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $S$ be its surface area. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ y & =4\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ z & =7\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-5\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =11\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} & =-5\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $S$ knowing the rate of change of $x,$ $y$ and $z.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2xz+2xy+2yz) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =(2x+2y)(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})+(2x+2z)(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+(2z+2y)(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =(2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4)(-5)+(2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 7)(11)+(2\\cdot 7+2\\cdot 4)(-5) \\\\  & =-60+198-110 \\\\  & =28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area of the solid is increasing at a rate of $28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-360e3f58-2f52-52b9-85ca-0ee548100f6f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-360e3f58-2f52-52b9-85ca-0ee548100f6f" :answer-field/id #uuid "360e3f58-2f52-52b9-85ca-0ee548100f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a44857f-c227-5ee8-907e-759c13f62a60" :answer-field/choices ["answer-123f9b2b-0563-52eb-a8a6-c11e35140af8" "answer-ee63a80b-6b4b-5e42-89f8-7c9624056a03" "answer-31c4c2e2-f9c7-55fa-9b0b-965e7a60983f" "answer-d4901436-e9f5-5dcb-ad95-a9bd329e5817" "answer-6a44857f-c227-5ee8-907e-759c13f62a60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-123f9b2b-0563-52eb-a8a6-c11e35140af8" :answer/id #uuid "123f9b2b-0563-52eb-a8a6-c11e35140af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee63a80b-6b4b-5e42-89f8-7c9624056a03" :answer/id #uuid "ee63a80b-6b4b-5e42-89f8-7c9624056a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31c4c2e2-f9c7-55fa-9b0b-965e7a60983f" :answer/id #uuid "31c4c2e2-f9c7-55fa-9b0b-965e7a60983f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4901436-e9f5-5dcb-ad95-a9bd329e5817" :answer/id #uuid "d4901436-e9f5-5dcb-ad95-a9bd329e5817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a44857f-c227-5ee8-907e-759c13f62a60" :answer/id #uuid "6a44857f-c227-5ee8-907e-759c13f62a60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4e4521f6-9e6d-5c0e-807a-ed8494a208e7" :question/id #uuid "4e4521f6-9e6d-5c0e-807a-ed8494a208e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-2775" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7aad5aea708422b331b19ab2e9c7586b5b037054347841530db829e2fc3c9075.png)\n\nIf the surface area of a cube is increasing at a rate of $48{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\text{/s},$ at what rate are the edges changing when each edge is $2\\text{ cm}?$ Assume that each edge is increasing at the same rate." :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the side of the cube, let $S$ be its surface area, and let $V$ be its volume. All of the variables change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=48\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $x$ knowing the rate of change of $S.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the cube:\n\n$$\nS=6{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(S) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 48 & =12(2)\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the edges are changing at a rate of $2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5d9ddee8-9080-52f3-b380-7069a58028d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5d9ddee8-9080-52f3-b380-7069a58028d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d9ddee8-9080-52f3-b380-7069a58028d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f20456ef-886c-5102-993e-3508d86e67a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77e02e51-9520-5960-af4b-5e7149ff91fe" "answer-da1699ce-9cb8-5975-b914-ea145e4e7b1c" "answer-f20456ef-886c-5102-993e-3508d86e67a4" "answer-e96e67b0-5d53-5ccd-92b7-40b07cd5c7a7" "answer-f4b001ca-ac85-5dbf-8676-ca2181df987d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77e02e51-9520-5960-af4b-5e7149ff91fe" :answer/id #uuid "77e02e51-9520-5960-af4b-5e7149ff91fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da1699ce-9cb8-5975-b914-ea145e4e7b1c" :answer/id #uuid "da1699ce-9cb8-5975-b914-ea145e4e7b1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f20456ef-886c-5102-993e-3508d86e67a4" :answer/id #uuid "f20456ef-886c-5102-993e-3508d86e67a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e96e67b0-5d53-5ccd-92b7-40b07cd5c7a7" :answer/id #uuid "e96e67b0-5d53-5ccd-92b7-40b07cd5c7a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4b001ca-ac85-5dbf-8676-ca2181df987d" :answer/id #uuid "f4b001ca-ac85-5dbf-8676-ca2181df987d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2d8efcf9-a827-5e33-8982-8c950b1390fe" :question/id #uuid "2d8efcf9-a827-5e33-8982-8c950b1390fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-30081" :question/problem "![](images/ea/ea7c818a6694ba959c5230dcde8611a7b1dc44bcad383f54c93d2934336c35b6.png)\n\nThe edges of a cube decrease at a rate of $9\\text{ cm/s}.$ At what rate is the volume decreasing when the length of each edge is $40\\text{ cm}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the side length of the cube and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-9\\text{ cm/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=40\\text{ cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the cube:\n\n$$\nV={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug $x=40$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-9\\text{ cm/s}$ into the expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =3(40)^{2}\\cdot (-9)\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-43\\,200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the cube is decreasing at a rate of $43\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}$ at the moment when $x=40\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7049e9d7-8f84-594a-912b-f5fcab69cbfa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7049e9d7-8f84-594a-912b-f5fcab69cbfa" :answer-field/id #uuid "7049e9d7-8f84-594a-912b-f5fcab69cbfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1d66b81f-aab7-5dee-bc76-93149d565137" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70ef183c-3e32-589d-bdef-3a17eb486140" "answer-c387d300-dcb3-5156-be2d-bccac09b58bc" "answer-0d1b4802-4fbf-597a-8717-edd9da5ff601" "answer-1d66b81f-aab7-5dee-bc76-93149d565137" "answer-651e5094-ed0f-5287-afa0-88760a288cd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70ef183c-3e32-589d-bdef-3a17eb486140" :answer/id #uuid "70ef183c-3e32-589d-bdef-3a17eb486140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40\\,150{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c387d300-dcb3-5156-be2d-bccac09b58bc" :answer/id #uuid "c387d300-dcb3-5156-be2d-bccac09b58bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d1b4802-4fbf-597a-8717-edd9da5ff601" :answer/id #uuid "0d1b4802-4fbf-597a-8717-edd9da5ff601" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d66b81f-aab7-5dee-bc76-93149d565137" :answer/id #uuid "1d66b81f-aab7-5dee-bc76-93149d565137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-651e5094-ed0f-5287-afa0-88760a288cd1" :answer/id #uuid "651e5094-ed0f-5287-afa0-88760a288cd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44\\,100{\\text{ cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-94a70c07-52ed-54e0-b434-f6f0663ba853" :question/id #uuid "94a70c07-52ed-54e0-b434-f6f0663ba853" :question/math-academy-id "q-314534" :question/problem "![](images/81/81175de5197dac2f2f037bde6985be619c68de75a574853c61de75316ae63971.png)\n\nA rectangular swimming pool is being drained. If its length and width are $32\\text{ m}$ and $12\\text{ m}$, respectively, and the water level is falling at a rate of $0.4\\,\\text{m/min},$ how fast is the water draining out of the pool? Assume that the drain rate is positive and do not round the answer.\n\nThe water is draining out at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/min}.$" :question/worked-solution "We define the following variables:\n\n- let $L$ and $W$ be the length and width of the swimming pool, respectively, and\n\n- let $h$ and $V$ be the height and volume of the water, respectively.\n\nNote that $h$ and $V$ change with time, while $L$ and $W$ are constants. \n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nL=32\\,\\text{m},\\,W=12\\,\\text{m},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=-0.4\\,\\text{m}/\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of water:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of $V=LWh$ with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}V & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(32)(12)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =384\\cdot (-0.4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-153.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water is draining out at a rate of $153.6\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9eb3869d-baa4-5c43-ac49-35af5641a53b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9eb3869d-baa4-5c43-ac49-35af5641a53b" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb3869d-baa4-5c43-ac49-35af5641a53b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cfb0f980-6010-5ae0-ac8a-7691fa64a449" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cfb0f980-6010-5ae0-ac8a-7691fa64a449"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfb0f980-6010-5ae0-ac8a-7691fa64a449" :answer/id #uuid "cfb0f980-6010-5ae0-ac8a-7691fa64a449" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "153.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064724 :question/problem "![](images/f5/f504ea91bae5d27b3e7b31d697ed06c9e34d838724e8dafac46e69d84de9c3cf.png)\n\nA gas station has a rectangular gasoline storage tank stored underground. The tank is $15\\text{ feet}$ long and $10\\text{ feet}$ wide. A worker lowers a dip stick into the tank and notices that the depth of the gasoline is decreasing by $2\\text{ feet}$ every hour. How fast is the volume of gasoline decreasing?" :question/worked-solution "We define the following variables:\n\n- let $L$ and $W$ be the length and width of the tank, respectively, and\n\n- let $h$ and $V$ be the height and volume of the gasoline in the tank, respectively.\n\nNote that $h$ and $V$ change with time, while $L$ and $W$ are constants. \n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nL=15\\,\\text{ft},\\,W=10\\,\\text{ft},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=-2\\,\\text{ft}/\\text{hour}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of the gasoline in the tank:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of $V=LWh$ with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}V & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(15)(10)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =150\\cdot (-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-300.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gasoline level is decreasing at a rate of $300\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}\\text{/hour}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186062401 :answer-field/correct "answer-5c8adc1b-e870-5266-9de9-84b7d51f9fef" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4f841d86-51bb-5ddc-8524-7fe2a6b1ca71" "answer-5c8adc1b-e870-5266-9de9-84b7d51f9fef" "answer-d7cfb825-dab5-5d3d-a6ab-f334d5939ed7" "answer-5c73fdcc-2e08-5492-82ae-b65c09e57968" "answer-275c62d3-3e00-52d0-9d98-f55885e3b40d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f841d86-51bb-5ddc-8524-7fe2a6b1ca71" :answer/id #uuid "4f841d86-51bb-5ddc-8524-7fe2a6b1ca71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "240\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c8adc1b-e870-5266-9de9-84b7d51f9fef" :answer/id #uuid "5c8adc1b-e870-5266-9de9-84b7d51f9fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7cfb825-dab5-5d3d-a6ab-f334d5939ed7" :answer/id #uuid "d7cfb825-dab5-5d3d-a6ab-f334d5939ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "360\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c73fdcc-2e08-5492-82ae-b65c09e57968" :answer/id #uuid "5c73fdcc-2e08-5492-82ae-b65c09e57968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "400\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-275c62d3-3e00-52d0-9d98-f55885e3b40d" :answer/id #uuid "275c62d3-3e00-52d0-9d98-f55885e3b40d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "440\\,{\\text{feet}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dd9599f1-ed67-5948-967c-4c445ad154d3" :question/id #uuid "dd9599f1-ed67-5948-967c-4c445ad154d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-49012" :question/problem "![](images/06/06eb8269e36ecb0185c0bfa0069c36a705e36711ca0a705fba3e6eae7b6c946d.png)\n\nJohn is a carpenter who wants to modify a wooden box. The length, width and height of the box are decreased at a rate of $1\\text{ cm/s},$ $2\\text{ cm/s}$ and $4\\text{ cm/s},$ respectively. Determine the rate at which the volume of the box decreases, if its dimensions are $15\\text{ cm}$ long, $10\\text{ cm}$ wide and $15\\text{ cm}$ high." :question/worked-solution "Let $L,$ $W,$ $H$ and $V$ be the length, the width, the height, and the volume of the box, respectively. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L=15\\text{ cm},\\, & W=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ H=15\\text{ cm},\\, & \\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-1\\text{ cm/s}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2\\text{ cm/s},\\, & \\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\text{ cm/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the four variables is given by the formula for the volume of a rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=LWH\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of $V=LWH$ with respect to $t,$ using the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}V & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWH) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =W\\cdot H(\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t})+L\\cdot H(\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t})+L\\cdot W(\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(10)(15)(-1)+(15)(15)(-2)+(15)(10)(-4) \\\\  & =-1\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the box is decreasing at a rate of $1\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1d21bae5-4b6c-54e9-aab3-a599790bd158"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1d21bae5-4b6c-54e9-aab3-a599790bd158" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d21bae5-4b6c-54e9-aab3-a599790bd158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-864515c1-3b8e-59c9-b866-916b8262d2d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-864515c1-3b8e-59c9-b866-916b8262d2d5" "answer-88a9531f-3fb7-5eed-9a5e-1179bfcc6d8e" "answer-1d2ce6b1-c4fc-5ed8-8a4c-3a4c5f749dd2" "answer-c5a2b408-e5cd-52e5-aaa7-f0316c914927" "answer-16d6b89b-9c2e-5338-b504-d4c40283ef6f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-864515c1-3b8e-59c9-b866-916b8262d2d5" :answer/id #uuid "864515c1-3b8e-59c9-b866-916b8262d2d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,200{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88a9531f-3fb7-5eed-9a5e-1179bfcc6d8e" :answer/id #uuid "88a9531f-3fb7-5eed-9a5e-1179bfcc6d8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,750{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d2ce6b1-c4fc-5ed8-8a4c-3a4c5f749dd2" :answer/id #uuid "1d2ce6b1-c4fc-5ed8-8a4c-3a4c5f749dd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "525{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5a2b408-e5cd-52e5-aaa7-f0316c914927" :answer/id #uuid "c5a2b408-e5cd-52e5-aaa7-f0316c914927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "670{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16d6b89b-9c2e-5338-b504-d4c40283ef6f" :answer/id #uuid "16d6b89b-9c2e-5338-b504-d4c40283ef6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "820{\\text{ cm}}^{3}/\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-68f6bf29-8273-5b7e-a834-752eee067f78" :question/id #uuid "68f6bf29-8273-5b7e-a834-752eee067f78" :question/math-academy-id "q-343321" :question/problem "![](images/ba/baa2d9cf6ae9d34de744374dbfe67e44589aa9331c1391e5fc168cd6a39bca4d.png)\n\nJennie fills an aquarium, in the shape of a rectangular prism that is $50\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $25\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, with water from a tap. How fast is the volume of water in the aquarium changing if the water level is rising at a rate of $0.2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{h}?$\n\nThe volume of water in the aquarium is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/h}.$" :question/worked-solution "We define the following variables:\n\n- let $L$ and $W$ be the length and width of the aquarium, respectively, and\n\n- let $h$ and $V$ be the height and volume of the water, respectively.\n\nNote that $h$ and $V$ change with time, while $L$ and $W$ are constants. \n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nL=50\\,\\text{m},\\,W=25\\,\\text{m},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=0.2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of water:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of $V=LWh$ with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}V & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(50)(25)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =1250\\cdot 0.2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =250.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of water in the aquarium is increasing at a rate of $250\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-abea57b7-3c7f-5d2e-8706-848858e9de5a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-abea57b7-3c7f-5d2e-8706-848858e9de5a" :answer-field/id #uuid "abea57b7-3c7f-5d2e-8706-848858e9de5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d5e820f6-11e5-54c5-8711-692747bbbe70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d5e820f6-11e5-54c5-8711-692747bbbe70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e820f6-11e5-54c5-8711-692747bbbe70" :answer/id #uuid "d5e820f6-11e5-54c5-8711-692747bbbe70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064452 :activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179631 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ab1f13b6-54f8-513e-bf58-990f13684639" "question-6a919522-1a8b-510f-a55a-40d3694f3593" "question-7a0740d0-7284-503e-8e76-e4838bad99ae" "question-1bd18cb1-6693-5a86-9b4f-9983e714337e" "question-71608d79-53e7-5fb6-8d93-2ff0a25b9a99"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179474 :question/problem "What is the slope of the line $4x-2y=1?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2y & =1 \\\\ -2y & =-4x+1 \\\\ 2y & =4x-1 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{2} & =\\frac{4x-1}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y & =2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179632 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f153c106-d98f-5f2d-af98-3aa7927bfc4d" "question-6b2df9ca-452f-5057-9208-dd46b2f5dde7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179475 :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercept, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $x.$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t4x-3y&=8\\[5pt]\n\t4x-3(0)&=8\\[5pt]\n\t4x&=8\\[5pt]\n\t\\dfrac{4x}{4}&=\\dfrac{8}{4}\\[5pt]\n\tx&=2\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $2,$ and we conclude that the line intersects the $x$-axis at $\\left(2,0\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179633 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-00f5442f-d34a-5776-aee4-863c683c730e" "question-eaf53385-8d80-57b1-9850-e91d1aa3e647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179476 :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation and solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-4y & =-8 \\\\ 5(0)-4y & =-8 \\\\ -4y & =-8 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $2,$ and we conclude that the line intersects the $y$-axis at $\\left(0,2\\right).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab1f13b6-54f8-513e-bf58-990f13684639" :question/id #uuid "ab1f13b6-54f8-513e-bf58-990f13684639" :question/math-academy-id "q-214666" :question/problem "What is the slope of the line $-4x=5?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x & =5 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the line is vertical, and its slope is undefined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cda38b41-bd8e-54cc-8085-8d3dd26c9eba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cda38b41-bd8e-54cc-8085-8d3dd26c9eba" :answer-field/id #uuid "cda38b41-bd8e-54cc-8085-8d3dd26c9eba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eceac2af-a4fe-5072-8c46-0ed3cf09b1c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c29b84c9-927f-51e4-9aca-f6615380de8a" "answer-643a28c9-1ba7-51f8-b7ab-516a3b9fa3ec" "answer-af4e63ae-c53f-540c-a59d-4dd3d63a74b9" "answer-bb5968b0-286c-50a7-9eef-f3a0f72b8873" "answer-eceac2af-a4fe-5072-8c46-0ed3cf09b1c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c29b84c9-927f-51e4-9aca-f6615380de8a" :answer/id #uuid "c29b84c9-927f-51e4-9aca-f6615380de8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-643a28c9-1ba7-51f8-b7ab-516a3b9fa3ec" :answer/id #uuid "643a28c9-1ba7-51f8-b7ab-516a3b9fa3ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af4e63ae-c53f-540c-a59d-4dd3d63a74b9" :answer/id #uuid "af4e63ae-c53f-540c-a59d-4dd3d63a74b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb5968b0-286c-50a7-9eef-f3a0f72b8873" :answer/id #uuid "bb5968b0-286c-50a7-9eef-f3a0f72b8873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eceac2af-a4fe-5072-8c46-0ed3cf09b1c0" :answer/id #uuid "eceac2af-a4fe-5072-8c46-0ed3cf09b1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The slope is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a919522-1a8b-510f-a55a-40d3694f3593" :question/id #uuid "6a919522-1a8b-510f-a55a-40d3694f3593" :question/math-academy-id "q-214668" :question/problem "What is the slope of the line $4x+7=0?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+7 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-7 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the line is vertical, and its slope is undefined." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-07ffe521-b249-5aa0-b4b1-011add1acd46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07ffe521-b249-5aa0-b4b1-011add1acd46" :answer-field/id #uuid "07ffe521-b249-5aa0-b4b1-011add1acd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a4a6b940-1938-56ce-84ce-7600146a9d3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2969dd43-fdac-561b-8c1d-4ecc5b15511d" "answer-40fb9073-cdb7-53e8-ad67-7269eea14711" "answer-70a0daf1-462a-543b-a8d3-ac4eb8f659c1" "answer-a46e0df7-ee30-5da9-aa2f-3a089627307d" "answer-a4a6b940-1938-56ce-84ce-7600146a9d3e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2969dd43-fdac-561b-8c1d-4ecc5b15511d" :answer/id #uuid "2969dd43-fdac-561b-8c1d-4ecc5b15511d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40fb9073-cdb7-53e8-ad67-7269eea14711" :answer/id #uuid "40fb9073-cdb7-53e8-ad67-7269eea14711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70a0daf1-462a-543b-a8d3-ac4eb8f659c1" :answer/id #uuid "70a0daf1-462a-543b-a8d3-ac4eb8f659c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a46e0df7-ee30-5da9-aa2f-3a089627307d" :answer/id #uuid "a46e0df7-ee30-5da9-aa2f-3a089627307d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4a6b940-1938-56ce-84ce-7600146a9d3e" :answer/id #uuid "a4a6b940-1938-56ce-84ce-7600146a9d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The slope is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7a0740d0-7284-503e-8e76-e4838bad99ae" :question/id #uuid "7a0740d0-7284-503e-8e76-e4838bad99ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-22787" :question/problem "What is the slope of the line $2x+5y=1?$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the slope of the line if we can express its equation in slope-intercept form. To do this, we solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =1 \\\\ 5y & =-2x+1 \\\\ \\frac{5y}{5} & =\\frac{-2x+1}{5} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2x}{5}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}x+\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the slope-intercept equation, we can tell that the slope of the line is $m=-\\frac{2}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77ba2dc0-680e-51f7-8e6e-8be3d8e551c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77ba2dc0-680e-51f7-8e6e-8be3d8e551c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "77ba2dc0-680e-51f7-8e6e-8be3d8e551c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-de039c45-265b-503b-ba6d-4b7d1befdbc8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2239c35e-3145-5856-af94-fd5581d244c3" "answer-de039c45-265b-503b-ba6d-4b7d1befdbc8" "answer-32a0b2e3-cb3a-5d86-bff5-04580915b914" "answer-c6f9543f-3213-547b-98d1-950edaa18467" "answer-3d807d89-059f-51ec-8960-748837a3c2a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2239c35e-3145-5856-af94-fd5581d244c3" :answer/id #uuid "2239c35e-3145-5856-af94-fd5581d244c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de039c45-265b-503b-ba6d-4b7d1befdbc8" :answer/id #uuid "de039c45-265b-503b-ba6d-4b7d1befdbc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32a0b2e3-cb3a-5d86-bff5-04580915b914" :answer/id #uuid "32a0b2e3-cb3a-5d86-bff5-04580915b914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6f9543f-3213-547b-98d1-950edaa18467" :answer/id #uuid "c6f9543f-3213-547b-98d1-950edaa18467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d807d89-059f-51ec-8960-748837a3c2a3" :answer/id #uuid "3d807d89-059f