have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),\\,2t+4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c8c2630-d3ad-5f34-b976-b9b1cdd286bf" "answer-field-41888a9a-6a30-5987-80e4-7c935376e015"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c8c2630-d3ad-5f34-b976-b9b1cdd286bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8c2630-d3ad-5f34-b976-b9b1cdd286bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee" :answer/id #uuid "92705079-d79b-5261-951a-6c24a139f8ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41888a9a-6a30-5987-80e4-7c935376e015" :answer-field/id #uuid "41888a9a-6a30-5987-80e4-7c935376e015" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053" :answer/id #uuid "e8ebedb0-f624-5092-8452-0e8ea51ac053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-19691404-0bb9-5165-a3cc-ce9a79557b1b" :question/id #uuid "19691404-0bb9-5165-a3cc-ce9a79557b1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349464" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-7t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=3{t}^{4}-7t+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{3}-7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{3}-7,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-076d86ba-a029-593b-a409-24685a0fec46" "answer-field-b0c96d28-1366-5868-a326-9af707a402ca"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-076d86ba-a029-593b-a409-24685a0fec46" :answer-field/id #uuid "076d86ba-a029-593b-a409-24685a0fec46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e" :answer/id #uuid "6736b43c-00dc-58a4-b07e-13bb811a478e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{t}^{3}-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b0c96d28-1366-5868-a326-9af707a402ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0c96d28-1366-5868-a326-9af707a402ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c" :answer/id #uuid "c6135c28-1b5c-55ad-9ba6-dfb9a75e1b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bf645e6-f706-50ea-8450-5ddbc0499160" :question/id #uuid "2bf645e6-f706-50ea-8450-5ddbc0499160" :question/math-academy-id "q-50377" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4t-10,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d97608c5-ec21-5589-b8cb-89d769aeba4d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d97608c5-ec21-5589-b8cb-89d769aeba4d" :answer-field/id #uuid "d97608c5-ec21-5589-b8cb-89d769aeba4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff20f98e-9f1b-5ada-b97d-a2fe856607b6" "answer-4eee71c6-18a3-564f-aef0-94f6b2a849b1" "answer-67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" "answer-06006b25-a443-54f2-8024-d157cc2b8a3d" "answer-da6cdfe0-793c-5d04-b91f-02dd3f4e71ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff20f98e-9f1b-5ada-b97d-a2fe856607b6" :answer/id #uuid "ff20f98e-9f1b-5ada-b97d-a2fe856607b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eee71c6-18a3-564f-aef0-94f6b2a849b1" :answer/id #uuid "4eee71c6-18a3-564f-aef0-94f6b2a849b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{3t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/id #uuid "67188f0b-4321-5aa6-8b40-a0a721632c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06006b25-a443-54f2-8024-d157cc2b8a3d" :answer/id #uuid "06006b25-a443-54f2-8024-d157cc2b8a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da6cdfe0-793c-5d04-b91f-02dd3f4e71ec" :answer/id #uuid "da6cdfe0-793c-5d04-b91f-02dd3f4e71ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨t,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66e3887f-e0ed-593b-b271-ae704cd5f2f1" :question/id #uuid "66e3887f-e0ed-593b-b271-ae704cd5f2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-34720" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9f0a5f53-2383-5407-951d-8f444396db3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f0a5f53-2383-5407-951d-8f444396db3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f0a5f53-2383-5407-951d-8f444396db3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-594d297d-4ffa-5fcd-8767-7af6f4ed264d" "answer-c255f2ae-f1e7-5320-99a1-222b7be0cc5b" "answer-c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" "answer-82e99160-4a68-56e8-a3ef-7b8309c26551" "answer-7e43eea9-78bb-565d-8191-43c478367b3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-594d297d-4ffa-5fcd-8767-7af6f4ed264d" :answer/id #uuid "594d297d-4ffa-5fcd-8767-7af6f4ed264d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c255f2ae-f1e7-5320-99a1-222b7be0cc5b" :answer/id #uuid "c255f2ae-f1e7-5320-99a1-222b7be0cc5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" :answer/id #uuid "c78884eb-c06b-51c6-b4c7-0f6e4cc6678d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e99160-4a68-56e8-a3ef-7b8309c26551" :answer/id #uuid "82e99160-4a68-56e8-a3ef-7b8309c26551" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j-\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e43eea9-78bb-565d-8191-43c478367b3c" :answer/id #uuid "7e43eea9-78bb-565d-8191-43c478367b3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-87416abb-dad9-5afe-bb9d-e8fcd5a9095c" :question/id #uuid "87416abb-dad9-5afe-bb9d-e8fcd5a9095c" :question/math-academy-id "q-350227" :question/problem "Given that  $f(t)=2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)\\,i-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\frac{6}{t}\\,k,$   what is ${f}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t))\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{6}{t})\\,k \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot 1)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\,j-\\frac{6}{{1}^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡1\\,j-6\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0bfa90a3-ba24-559f-9c8b-5a07e671e7fb" "answer-field-f4dc9af4-ea47-5fb1-8da7-ddafaed28423" "answer-field-504d5d52-6b4f-57e5-9c75-2dca13703f87"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0bfa90a3-ba24-559f-9c8b-5a07e671e7fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bfa90a3-ba24-559f-9c8b-5a07e671e7fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8eec3fb3-98bb-539f-828a-96203367f774" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8eec3fb3-98bb-539f-828a-96203367f774"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eec3fb3-98bb-539f-828a-96203367f774" :answer/id #uuid "8eec3fb3-98bb-539f-828a-96203367f774" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\ln(3)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f4dc9af4-ea47-5fb1-8da7-ddafaed28423" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4dc9af4-ea47-5fb1-8da7-ddafaed28423" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8" :answer/id #uuid "bc780555-5bb0-55aa-b97f-a47fa4610bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cos(1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-504d5d52-6b4f-57e5-9c75-2dca13703f87" :answer-field/id #uuid "504d5d52-6b4f-57e5-9c75-2dca13703f87" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc" :answer/id #uuid "11cf7146-ed56-5694-a708-a9b3016a6fdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0cc15b80-72fe-59a5-9238-583abab2565e" :question/id #uuid "0cc15b80-72fe-59a5-9238-583abab2565e" :question/math-academy-id "q-350802" :question/problem "Determine ${f}^{″}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{t} \\\\ {e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -2{t}^{6}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{″}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{1-2t})\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{6})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ -2{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -12{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{e}^{1-2t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12{t}^{5})\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3/2}} \\\\ 4{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -60{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd2548aa-0d72-568a-936f-6eb2f6da4f5c" "answer-field-d0de4306-091e-529b-ae8c-530f65ea903f" "answer-field-9181ccb7-fad9-5675-90e4-730835fd6807"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd2548aa-0d72-568a-936f-6eb2f6da4f5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd2548aa-0d72-568a-936f-6eb2f6da4f5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf" :answer/id #uuid "51e9395c-263f-51bd-b6a4-d472df228bdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{t^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d0de4306-091e-529b-ae8c-530f65ea903f" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0de4306-091e-529b-ae8c-530f65ea903f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166" :answer/id #uuid "3300ef54-fdde-5f40-809c-0c4bab2d0166" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e^{1-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9181ccb7-fad9-5675-90e4-730835fd6807" :answer-field/id #uuid "9181ccb7-fad9-5675-90e4-730835fd6807" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d" :answer/id #uuid "61d7cc13-045d-5dfc-8f21-557e9035974d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60t^4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb16de2e-8644-5cec-a8df-6022a66874f3" :question/id #uuid "eb16de2e-8644-5cec-a8df-6022a66874f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-347967" :question/problem "Determine ${f}^{″}(t)$ given that $f(t)={e}^{5-2t}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,j-3{t}^{4}\\,k.$\n\n${f}^{″}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{5-2t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =-2{e}^{5-2t}\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\,j-12{t}^{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{e}^{5-2t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12{t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =-2(-2{e}^{5-2t})\\,i+3(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\,j-12(3{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =4{e}^{5-2t}\\,i-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,j-36{t}^{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3d407d0c-c934-570f-b937-ad8a2b67c857" "answer-field-71566823-fdda-54f3-9974-db4a29c8e963" "answer-field-9b71e92c-1904-5ed5-a643-9f6e96a86f83"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d407d0c-c934-570f-b937-ad8a2b67c857" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d407d0c-c934-570f-b937-ad8a2b67c857" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e24d1ecc-57dc-5c33-9cba-5e409dfc2302" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e24d1ecc-57dc-5c33-9cba-5e409dfc2302"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e24d1ecc-57dc-5c33-9cba-5e409dfc2302" :answer/id #uuid "e24d1ecc-57dc-5c33-9cba-5e409dfc2302" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e^{5-2t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-71566823-fdda-54f3-9974-db4a29c8e963" :answer-field/id #uuid "71566823-fdda-54f3-9974-db4a29c8e963" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1d3bbfad-8739-5e99-a5ae-7f7260792e57" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d3bbfad-8739-5e99-a5ae-7f7260792e57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d3bbfad-8739-5e99-a5ae-7f7260792e57" :answer/id #uuid "1d3bbfad-8739-5e99-a5ae-7f7260792e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\sin(3t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b71e92c-1904-5ed5-a643-9f6e96a86f83" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b71e92c-1904-5ed5-a643-9f6e96a86f83" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-4529e2b9-bc07-531e-b375-674552dad476" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4529e2b9-bc07-531e-b375-674552dad476"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4529e2b9-bc07-531e-b375-674552dad476" :answer/id #uuid "4529e2b9-bc07-531e-b375-674552dad476" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36t^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b01d0b7-5c1a-5382-b422-a24594a7e8ee" :question/id #uuid "8b01d0b7-5c1a-5382-b422-a24594a7e8ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-75033" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}-t,\\,7t-3{t}^{4}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=4{t}^{3}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =12{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=7t-3{t}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =7-12{t}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-36{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ad618895-a9b2-5479-91a2-b7889155fabf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ad618895-a9b2-5479-91a2-b7889155fabf" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad618895-a9b2-5479-91a2-b7889155fabf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce607db8-3e5f-5aee-be46-05f404a110b9" "answer-4aa25a3e-ad0c-5469-b35f-f6b463e1bf29" "answer-6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" "answer-4de7e70a-49ca-5324-89ae-72cc0b88d9c0" "answer-1655080f-c794-53f9-9762-71446a1428b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce607db8-3e5f-5aee-be46-05f404a110b9" :answer/id #uuid "ce607db8-3e5f-5aee-be46-05f404a110b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-36t,\\,24{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4aa25a3e-ad0c-5469-b35f-f6b463e1bf29" :answer/id #uuid "4aa25a3e-ad0c-5469-b35f-f6b463e1bf29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12t,\\,-12{t}^{3}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" :answer/id #uuid "6ec79135-6f74-58f5-be5f-857da38fc279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4de7e70a-49ca-5324-89ae-72cc0b88d9c0" :answer/id #uuid "4de7e70a-49ca-5324-89ae-72cc0b88d9c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨24{t}^{2},\\,36t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1655080f-c794-53f9-9762-71446a1428b5" :answer/id #uuid "1655080f-c794-53f9-9762-71446a1428b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨24{t}^{3},\\,16{t}^{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f415e47a-854d-5840-b197-b8e66cc67e42" :question/id #uuid "f415e47a-854d-5840-b197-b8e66cc67e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-34722" :question/problem "Calculate the second derivative of  $f(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩$ with respect to $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(s)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(s)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4afb8b57-1fee-58f6-a694-2fa66ad992b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4afb8b57-1fee-58f6-a694-2fa66ad992b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "4afb8b57-1fee-58f6-a694-2fa66ad992b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" "answer-21637f5f-66fc-5d10-9eec-a98e25102b49" "answer-c51b200a-ecff-5cd9-93e9-8afa94661d25" "answer-1b9fceca-75ad-51bc-ae92-c08f9fc2becc" "answer-5e8fe481-3298-52af-9b2d-8bc1094ba831"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" :answer/id #uuid "85151a70-250f-5968-b519-91999091ac9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21637f5f-66fc-5d10-9eec-a98e25102b49" :answer/id #uuid "21637f5f-66fc-5d10-9eec-a98e25102b49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c51b200a-ecff-5cd9-93e9-8afa94661d25" :answer/id #uuid "c51b200a-ecff-5cd9-93e9-8afa94661d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡4s⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b9fceca-75ad-51bc-ae92-c08f9fc2becc" :answer/id #uuid "1b9fceca-75ad-51bc-ae92-c08f9fc2becc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e8fe481-3298-52af-9b2d-8bc1094ba831" :answer/id #uuid "5e8fe481-3298-52af-9b2d-8bc1094ba831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,16\\operatorname{cos}⁡4s⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199449 :tutorial/content "We can differentiate vector-valued functions with three components in the same way. \n\nFor example, if \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t) = \\big\\langle x(t), \\: y(t), \\: z(t) \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nis our vector-valued function, then the derivative is computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\text{d}\\mathbf{f}}{\\text{d}t} = \\left\\langle \\dfrac{ \\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}, \\: \\dfrac{ \\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\n \n\nFor example, suppose that we are given the vector function \n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\left\\langle t^3, \\:  \\ln(t+3), \\:  \\sqrt{t}\\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\n \n\nTo compute the derivative $\\mathbf f'\\!(t),$ we find the derivative of each component function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{d}{dt}⟨{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3),\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{d}{dt}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3)),\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+3},\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198483 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186171555 :answer-field/choices 17592186171556] [:db/retract 17592186171555 :answer-field/choices 17592186171557] [:db/retract 17592186171555 :answer-field/choices 17592186171558] [:db/retract 17592186171555 :answer-field/choices 17592186171559] [:db/retract 17592186171555 :answer-field/choices 17592186171560] {:db/id 17592186172044 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5b5c204f-7839-5ec6-95c0-a9151439158a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172655 :question/problem "A particle moves along a **clockwise** circular path with center $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $2\\pi \\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(3,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(3,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,3i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=3.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=3$ and $\\omega =-2\\pi \\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2\\pi t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi t)\\,j) \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171555 :answer-field/correct "answer-31e995dd-ff4a-5e6d-8cf4-3bfb96a6017b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0a4ff08-122d-5fd6-b066-879bdb9fa494" "answer-06716dfe-08a6-516e-a629-177bb828c2fa" "answer-3f2848b3-8ddd-5fb7-95ae-348cf52cb0ab" "answer-be530a2a-8d30-591a-8cf9-2082ebebbbb7" "answer-31e995dd-ff4a-5e6d-8cf4-3bfb96a6017b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0a4ff08-122d-5fd6-b066-879bdb9fa494" :answer/id #uuid "f0a4ff08-122d-5fd6-b066-879bdb9fa494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06716dfe-08a6-516e-a629-177bb828c2fa" :answer/id #uuid "06716dfe-08a6-516e-a629-177bb828c2fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=-3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f2848b3-8ddd-5fb7-95ae-348cf52cb0ab" :answer/id #uuid "3f2848b3-8ddd-5fb7-95ae-348cf52cb0ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be530a2a-8d30-591a-8cf9-2082ebebbbb7" :answer/id #uuid "be530a2a-8d30-591a-8cf9-2082ebebbbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e995dd-ff4a-5e6d-8cf4-3bfb96a6017b" :answer/id #uuid "31e995dd-ff4a-5e6d-8cf4-3bfb96a6017b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5b5c204f-7839-5ec6-95c0-a9151439158a" :question/id #uuid "5b5c204f-7839-5ec6-95c0-a9151439158a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97637" :question/problem "A particle moves along a **clockwise** circular path with center $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\text{ rad/s}.$ Given that the object is at the position $(1,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the position function of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nSince the object's initial position is $(1,0),$ we have that $r(0)=\\,1i,$ and we can conclude that the radius of the circle $R=1.$\n\nTherefore, since we have $R=1$ and $\\omega =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\text{ rad/s}$ (negative because the motion is clockwise), we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f20aec0-879d-5670-bfea-c9c0def60bdc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f20aec0-879d-5670-bfea-c9c0def60bdc" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f20aec0-879d-5670-bfea-c9c0def60bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e33da50a-6797-5e61-8dad-558084c1c0d5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9cde80f5-0a17-51cc-8fcb-e28702d3897c" "answer-43f6eebb-f90b-5e3e-bf7f-5a7b4d0e7ed4" "answer-05373043-ede4-5f3b-ab00-6c5eb28bd928" "answer-510f8649-056c-567e-b3ee-8b8aa7b327bd" "answer-e33da50a-6797-5e61-8dad-558084c1c0d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cde80f5-0a17-51cc-8fcb-e28702d3897c" :answer/id #uuid "9cde80f5-0a17-51cc-8fcb-e28702d3897c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43f6eebb-f90b-5e3e-bf7f-5a7b4d0e7ed4" :answer/id #uuid "43f6eebb-f90b-5e3e-bf7f-5a7b4d0e7ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05373043-ede4-5f3b-ab00-6c5eb28bd928" :answer/id #uuid "05373043-ede4-5f3b-ab00-6c5eb28bd928" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-510f8649-056c-567e-b3ee-8b8aa7b327bd" :answer/id #uuid "510f8649-056c-567e-b3ee-8b8aa7b327bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e33da50a-6797-5e61-8dad-558084c1c0d5" :answer/id #uuid "e33da50a-6797-5e61-8dad-558084c1c0d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2})\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172046 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea3775f0-4a19-53d1-b4e1-4eb3518e099f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea3775f0-4a19-53d1-b4e1-4eb3518e099f" :question/id #uuid "ea3775f0-4a19-53d1-b4e1-4eb3518e099f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97670" :question/problem "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j)$ meters. Find the magnitude of the acceleration of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =(v(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+9\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i-27\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the magnitude of the acceleration as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||a(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)^{2}+(-27\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{27}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡3t+{27}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡3t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{27}^{2}} \\\\  & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude of the acceleration is $27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nNote that $||a||$ is constant, but $a$ is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\na=-{\\omega }^{2}r\\,⇒\\,||a||={\\omega }^{2}||r||.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $a=3\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =3\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||a||={3}^{2}\\cdot 3=27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4264e826-1eca-5166-bc99-fe720168444a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4264e826-1eca-5166-bc99-fe720168444a" :answer-field/id #uuid "4264e826-1eca-5166-bc99-fe720168444a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a385d26b-a169-54eb-af49-c35e70069687" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f323c8b-a972-54d0-bbd1-34949e7b25d9" "answer-a385d26b-a169-54eb-af49-c35e70069687" "answer-0a682535-8c56-55dd-a035-f6b7cc19fc38" "answer-7be1cdf9-0f94-5f70-8486-f5416dfcc558" "answer-98ff3c6b-5897-5008-9dfd-a379593dd6c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f323c8b-a972-54d0-bbd1-34949e7b25d9" :answer/id #uuid "6f323c8b-a972-54d0-bbd1-34949e7b25d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a385d26b-a169-54eb-af49-c35e70069687" :answer/id #uuid "a385d26b-a169-54eb-af49-c35e70069687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a682535-8c56-55dd-a035-f6b7cc19fc38" :answer/id #uuid "0a682535-8c56-55dd-a035-f6b7cc19fc38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7be1cdf9-0f94-5f70-8486-f5416dfcc558" :answer/id #uuid "7be1cdf9-0f94-5f70-8486-f5416dfcc558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98ff3c6b-5897-5008-9dfd-a379593dd6c9" :answer/id #uuid "98ff3c6b-5897-5008-9dfd-a379593dd6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-948eb367-d5fd-51df-b125-e3149e49d0c4" :activity/id #uuid "948eb367-d5fd-51df-b125-e3149e49d0c4" :activity/title "Circular Motion About the Origin" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048656 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-368577ca-f476-5cfa-9e6b-273c753b6b1a" "step-b298bba9-5caf-53be-a1b8-5e5bfe3389e9" "step-c62d5c7d-4f34-5f60-92b7-d492ba362088" "step-7068fb21-64e6-51f4-b3a5-0162c383a600" "step-5c6597e4-8215-5ac5-9944-f088aeed0bde"] :activity/first-step "step-368577ca-f476-5cfa-9e6b-273c753b6b1a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-368577ca-f476-5cfa-9e6b-273c753b6b1a" :step/id #uuid "368577ca-f476-5cfa-9e6b-273c753b6b1a" :step/content 17592186172655 :step/next "step-b298bba9-5caf-53be-a1b8-5e5bfe3389e9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b298bba9-5caf-53be-a1b8-5e5bfe3389e9" :step/id #uuid "b298bba9-5caf-53be-a1b8-5e5bfe3389e9" :step/content 17592186362221 :step/next "step-c62d5c7d-4f34-5f60-92b7-d492ba362088" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c62d5c7d-4f34-5f60-92b7-d492ba362088" :step/id #uuid "c62d5c7d-4f34-5f60-92b7-d492ba362088" :step/content 17592186362222 :step/next "step-7068fb21-64e6-51f4-b3a5-0162c383a600" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7068fb21-64e6-51f4-b3a5-0162c383a600" :step/id #uuid "7068fb21-64e6-51f4-b3a5-0162c383a600" :step/content "question-5b5c204f-7839-5ec6-95c0-a9151439158a" :step/next "step-5c6597e4-8215-5ac5-9944-f088aeed0bde" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5c6597e4-8215-5ac5-9944-f088aeed0bde" :step/id #uuid "5c6597e4-8215-5ac5-9944-f088aeed0bde" :step/content "question-ea3775f0-4a19-53d1-b4e1-4eb3518e099f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147575 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b0060ce0-85fa-5c15-8314-02a2f37da794" "question-706f9bb5-de0a-5c75-aa53-ea495445a284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147148 :question/problem "If ![](images/18/18d57a5f075275e8b44ff372bbccb5677682ab13c3d316030da5410ab62343ad.svg) then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the part is $36,$ the percentage is $50\\%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $50\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{50}{100} = \\dfrac{50\\div 50}{100\\div 50} = \\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =36÷50% \\\\  & =36÷\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =36\\times \\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =36\\times 2 \\\\  & =72\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147576 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b23ca4fe-ec69-5d5b-b163-9360e0e9626e" "question-449615c3-fdfe-5f50-a3b0-a60b4eb31574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147149 :question/problem "$34\\%$ of a number is $170.$ What is the number?" :question/worked-solution "We're given that the part is $170,$ the percentage is $34\\%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $34\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{34}{100} = \\dfrac{34\\div 2}{100\\div 2} = \\dfrac{17}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =170÷34% \\\\  & =170÷\\frac{17}{50} \\\\  & =170\\times \\frac{50}{17} \\\\  & =\\frac{170}{17}\\times 50 \\\\  & =10\\times 50 \\\\  & =500\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147577 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-87c3bda2-8545-5669-83e3-84c3d08222b0" "question-b2281cf7-5deb-5971-96fe-4f78cb0692fd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147150 :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of girls in the math club, which is $16.$ The percentage is $40\\%,$ and the whole is the total number of club members.\n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $40\\%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{40}{100} = \\dfrac{40\\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =16÷40% \\\\  & =16÷\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =16\\times \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2}\\times 5 \\\\  & =8\\times 5 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the club has $40$ members." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b0060ce0-85fa-5c15-8314-02a2f37da794" :question/id #uuid "b0060ce0-85fa-5c15-8314-02a2f37da794" :question/math-academy-id "q-185091" :question/problem "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}$\\times \\,30%=24.$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $24,$ the percentage is $30%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $30%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=\\frac{30÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =24÷30% \\\\  & =24÷\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =24\\times \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3}\\times 10 \\\\  & =8\\times 10 \\\\  & =80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $80\\times 30%=24.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5201df42-972e-5151-bdcf-0c219c0c0b6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5201df42-972e-5151-bdcf-0c219c0c0b6d" :answer-field/id #uuid "5201df42-972e-5151-bdcf-0c219c0c0b6d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81" :answer/id #uuid "7203a599-e145-56ae-a118-e1542346dd81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-706f9bb5-de0a-5c75-aa53-ea495445a284" :question/id #uuid "706f9bb5-de0a-5c75-aa53-ea495445a284" :question/math-academy-id "q-160355" :question/problem "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 20%=14,$ then $\\,\\boxed{}=$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $14,$ the percentage is $20%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $20%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =14÷20% \\\\  & =14÷\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =14\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =14\\times 5 \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a60f895-e24e-53bc-9d51-27f66d1ee4cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a60f895-e24e-53bc-9d51-27f66d1ee4cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a60f895-e24e-53bc-9d51-27f66d1ee4cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0989f7fd-0593-51f1-ad5d-522251531367" "answer-487be039-8cee-556f-a591-54683cd090f4" "answer-671b3be1-5da4-5cf9-8892-6dde4b4dacdd" "answer-74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" "answer-ae45bd3b-76a6-5d21-9e72-9e93992e481c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0989f7fd-0593-51f1-ad5d-522251531367" :answer/id #uuid "0989f7fd-0593-51f1-ad5d-522251531367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-487be039-8cee-556f-a591-54683cd090f4" :answer/id #uuid "487be039-8cee-556f-a591-54683cd090f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-671b3be1-5da4-5cf9-8892-6dde4b4dacdd" :answer/id #uuid "671b3be1-5da4-5cf9-8892-6dde4b4dacdd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "62" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" :answer/id #uuid "74d23ef3-2cb1-5f88-a2da-701c7fa11d43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae45bd3b-76a6-5d21-9e72-9e93992e481c" :answer/id #uuid "ae45bd3b-76a6-5d21-9e72-9e93992e481c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "78" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b23ca4fe-ec69-5d5b-b163-9360e0e9626e" :question/id #uuid "b23ca4fe-ec69-5d5b-b163-9360e0e9626e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171157" :question/problem "$14%$ of{{field-1}}\nis $7.$" :question/worked-solution "The part is $7,$ the percentage is $14%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $14%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{100}=\\frac{14÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{7}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =7÷14% \\\\  & =7÷\\frac{7}{50} \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{50}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7}\\times 50 \\\\  & =1\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $14%$ of $50$ is $7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-646d465e-4f31-55a7-9533-68a3a82b8349"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-646d465e-4f31-55a7-9533-68a3a82b8349" :answer-field/id #uuid "646d465e-4f31-55a7-9533-68a3a82b8349" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6" :answer/id #uuid "a5e59494-db50-5c09-a591-ffc1049b89d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-449615c3-fdfe-5f50-a3b0-a60b4eb31574" :question/id #uuid "449615c3-fdfe-5f50-a3b0-a60b4eb31574" :question/math-academy-id "q-61300" :question/problem "If $\\,\\boxed{}\\times 25%=90,$ then what is the missing number?" :question/worked-solution "The part is $90,$ the percentage is $25%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\n \n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $25%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}=\\frac{25÷25}{100÷25}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =90÷25% \\\\  & =90÷\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =90\\times \\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =90\\times 4 \\\\  & =360\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3afa6d9f-7316-5ca5-8481-6c0db0d97e7d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3afa6d9f-7316-5ca5-8481-6c0db0d97e7d" :answer-field/id #uuid "3afa6d9f-7316-5ca5-8481-6c0db0d97e7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb93aefd-fe15-5f7f-96a3-d16e2cbef808" "answer-472c9925-e5fa-552e-bf38-58b1ee86cb75" "answer-2c26707e-2356-5432-a9e9-cb0c0034c30c" "answer-f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" "answer-a528645b-6270-574c-b026-6e64dc590071"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb93aefd-fe15-5f7f-96a3-d16e2cbef808" :answer/id #uuid "cb93aefd-fe15-5f7f-96a3-d16e2cbef808" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-472c9925-e5fa-552e-bf38-58b1ee86cb75" :answer/id #uuid "472c9925-e5fa-552e-bf38-58b1ee86cb75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1800" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c26707e-2356-5432-a9e9-cb0c0034c30c" :answer/id #uuid "2c26707e-2356-5432-a9e9-cb0c0034c30c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" :answer/id #uuid "f048a6d4-4633-5a87-b299-018587a58a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a528645b-6270-574c-b026-6e64dc590071" :answer/id #uuid "a528645b-6270-574c-b026-6e64dc590071" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-87c3bda2-8545-5669-83e3-84c3d08222b0" :question/id #uuid "87c3bda2-8545-5669-83e3-84c3d08222b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-61346" :question/problem "On a math test, Kevin answered $95%$ of the problems correctly. If he answered $38$ problems correctly, how many problems were on the test?" :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of problems answered correctly, which is $38.$ The percentage is $95%,$ and the whole is the total number of problems on the test. \n\nTo solve this question, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $95%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{95}{100}=\\frac{95÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{19}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =38÷95% \\\\  & =38÷\\frac{19}{20} \\\\  & =38\\times \\frac{20}{19} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{19}\\times 20 \\\\  & =2\\times 20 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there were $40$ problems on the test." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-848eb4e6-ce36-56ea-a0f1-8a1fe68b6389"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-848eb4e6-ce36-56ea-a0f1-8a1fe68b6389" :answer-field/id #uuid "848eb4e6-ce36-56ea-a0f1-8a1fe68b6389" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" "answer-856414f5-6bd6-5446-a194-c71a91eb1415" "answer-c1d57cb4-9cbb-5091-b7e4-afb49f54a805" "answer-b4c6e615-7f75-5019-a63a-1a7759574db8" "answer-91fd5ca4-51e8-5656-b5cc-97c65ac29624"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" :answer/id #uuid "0aec6150-9598-5e15-864d-cc269bf8d608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-856414f5-6bd6-5446-a194-c71a91eb1415" :answer/id #uuid "856414f5-6bd6-5446-a194-c71a91eb1415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1d57cb4-9cbb-5091-b7e4-afb49f54a805" :answer/id #uuid "c1d57cb4-9cbb-5091-b7e4-afb49f54a805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c6e615-7f75-5019-a63a-1a7759574db8" :answer/id #uuid "b4c6e615-7f75-5019-a63a-1a7759574db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91fd5ca4-51e8-5656-b5cc-97c65ac29624" :answer/id #uuid "91fd5ca4-51e8-5656-b5cc-97c65ac29624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2281cf7-5deb-5971-96fe-4f78cb0692fd" :question/id #uuid "b2281cf7-5deb-5971-96fe-4f78cb0692fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-61343" :question/problem "A school's softball team lost $18%$ of the games they played last year. If the team lost $9$ games last year, how many games did the team win?" :question/worked-solution "We need to know the total number of games played to determine the number of games won. \n\nWe're given a part and a percentage, and we need to find the whole.\n\nIn this case, the part is the number of games the team lost, which is $9.$ The percentage is $18%,$ and the whole is the total number of games played. \n\nTo find the whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $18%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{100}=\\frac{18÷2}{100÷2}=\\frac{9}{50}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =9÷18% \\\\  & =9÷\\frac{9}{50} \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{50}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}\\times 50 \\\\  & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played by the softball team last year was $50.$ The total number of games won is\n\n$$\n50-9=41.\n$$\n\nHence, the softball team won $41$ games last year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e4089d0-6e83-5bb9-a01d-10713a8e31b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e4089d0-6e83-5bb9-a01d-10713a8e31b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4089d0-6e83-5bb9-a01d-10713a8e31b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc1ca7bf-82a2-5e5e-8c98-5cf6337f7731" "answer-0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" "answer-ae3f93d0-753a-5489-8c3f-af8fc22cc58c" "answer-0bc1090e-61d0-5086-8900-d3ac3d3c7142" "answer-175774cc-bfba-5313-9d4b-4d00fbc5ce0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc1ca7bf-82a2-5e5e-8c98-5cf6337f7731" :answer/id #uuid "bc1ca7bf-82a2-5e5e-8c98-5cf6337f7731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" :answer/id #uuid "0ae02206-f280-552b-9c7e-f1b25280fec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae3f93d0-753a-5489-8c3f-af8fc22cc58c" :answer/id #uuid "ae3f93d0-753a-5489-8c3f-af8fc22cc58c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bc1090e-61d0-5086-8900-d3ac3d3c7142" :answer/id #uuid "0bc1090e-61d0-5086-8900-d3ac3d3c7142" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "51" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-175774cc-bfba-5313-9d4b-4d00fbc5ce0e" :answer/id #uuid "175774cc-bfba-5313-9d4b-4d00fbc5ce0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "61" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148781 :tutorial/content "To find a part given a percent and whole, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{percent} \\times \\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part}\n$$\n\nHowever, we sometimes want to find a whole given a part and a percent. To do this, we can use the relationship between multiplication and division to rewrite the above formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{whole} = \\textrm{part} \\div \\textrm{percent}\n$$\n\nLet's use this formula to find the missing number in the following statement:\n![](images/08/082c6ac53fa8de85b739dde0611943e92cb09d74d07378d6a33043d4b231e88d.svg)\n\nIn this case, the part is $540$, and the percent is $30\\%.$ \n\nWe can express $30\\%$ as a fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{30}{100} = \\dfrac{30\\div 10}{100\\div 10} = \\dfrac{3}{10}\n$$\n\nPutting these numbers into our formula for the whole, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =\\text{part}÷\\text{percent} \\\\  & =540÷30% \\\\  & =540÷\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =540\\times \\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{540}{3}\\times 10 \\\\  & =180\\times 10 \\\\  & =1,800\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $1,800.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147657 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179681 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cb6a3551-b7c8-5448-9dd7-361a94a204ac" "question-a4309379-1166-58a1-b1ee-b77ecf90fd3f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179540 :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $96x^5=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $x^5$ term and then taking the $5$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $x^5$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}96{x}^{5} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{5} & =\\frac{1}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $5$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=5$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5} & =\\frac{1}{32} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{5}} & =\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{1}{32}} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[5]{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{5}} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\dfrac12.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179680 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea193efd-d8e8-59fc-adc1-1d1595da20e0" "question-e173cb82-cae9-5da1-9ec4-a1b561689a6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179539 :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $5(x-6)^7 = 640.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x-6)^7$ term and then taking the $7$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x-6)^7$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-6)^{7} & =640 \\\\ (x-6)^{7} & =128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $7$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=7$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{7} & =128 \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{(x-6)^{7}} & =\\sqrt[7]{128} \\\\ x-6 & =\\sqrt[7]{{2}^{7}} \\\\ x-6 & =2 \\\\ x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=8.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb6a3551-b7c8-5448-9dd7-361a94a204ac" :question/id #uuid "cb6a3551-b7c8-5448-9dd7-361a94a204ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-111446" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{3}=-512.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =-512 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-512} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{(-8)^{3}} \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a526f7fb-2163-5bae-a670-b1a0e921b3ac"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a526f7fb-2163-5bae-a670-b1a0e921b3ac" :answer-field/id #uuid "a526f7fb-2163-5bae-a670-b1a0e921b3ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6267fb3f-a1e1-5114-a6e0-3d532383b112" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58ff20e3-a059-5a2b-b7c3-904742a44ac1" "answer-6267fb3f-a1e1-5114-a6e0-3d532383b112" "answer-d2964b1e-1e01-5aae-90ce-23893971c637" "answer-0ac74bf1-c829-5e81-ba8e-4fd203c6336e" "answer-9d4994a8-8333-5b8c-aaa0-7166a9d9eff9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58ff20e3-a059-5a2b-b7c3-904742a44ac1" :answer/id #uuid "58ff20e3-a059-5a2b-b7c3-904742a44ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6267fb3f-a1e1-5114-a6e0-3d532383b112" :answer/id #uuid "6267fb3f-a1e1-5114-a6e0-3d532383b112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2964b1e-1e01-5aae-90ce-23893971c637" :answer/id #uuid "d2964b1e-1e01-5aae-90ce-23893971c637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ac74bf1-c829-5e81-ba8e-4fd203c6336e" :answer/id #uuid "0ac74bf1-c829-5e81-ba8e-4fd203c6336e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4994a8-8333-5b8c-aaa0-7166a9d9eff9" :answer/id #uuid "9d4994a8-8333-5b8c-aaa0-7166a9d9eff9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no real solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a4309379-1166-58a1-b1ee-b77ecf90fd3f" :question/id #uuid "a4309379-1166-58a1-b1ee-b77ecf90fd3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-91347" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{3}=-343.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =-343 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-343} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{(-7)^{3}} \\\\ x & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28051cfe-f011-5fa7-a834-855cbe05e84c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28051cfe-f011-5fa7-a834-855cbe05e84c" :answer-field/id #uuid "28051cfe-f011-5fa7-a834-855cbe05e84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7560d60b-fe06-51f7-9bf9-6fae9c2eb5a9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af93c50c-2cba-5f1c-ac97-840c015e9e48" "answer-7560d60b-fe06-51f7-9bf9-6fae9c2eb5a9" "answer-c8762018-f421-5b66-87f4-e3b756aaf31b" "answer-67519f82-bf90-5eae-92ab-759d66a46d20" "answer-751c3f3c-6fe2-5175-b4e8-c998c19d82f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af93c50c-2cba-5f1c-ac97-840c015e9e48" :answer/id #uuid "af93c50c-2cba-5f1c-ac97-840c015e9e48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7560d60b-fe06-51f7-9bf9-6fae9c2eb5a9" :answer/id #uuid "7560d60b-fe06-51f7-9bf9-6fae9c2eb5a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8762018-f421-5b66-87f4-e3b756aaf31b" :answer/id #uuid "c8762018-f421-5b66-87f4-e3b756aaf31b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67519f82-bf90-5eae-92ab-759d66a46d20" :answer/id #uuid "67519f82-bf90-5eae-92ab-759d66a46d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-751c3f3c-6fe2-5175-b4e8-c998c19d82f9" :answer/id #uuid "751c3f3c-6fe2-5175-b4e8-c998c19d82f9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no real solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea193efd-d8e8-59fc-adc1-1d1595da20e0" :question/id #uuid "ea193efd-d8e8-59fc-adc1-1d1595da20e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111455" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $3(x+7)^{9}=1\\,536.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x+7)^{9}$ term and then taking the $9$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x+7)^{9}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+7)^{9} & =1\\,536 \\\\ (x+7)^{9} & =512\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $9$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since $n=9$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+7)^{9} & =512 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{(x+7)^{9}} & =\\sqrt[9]{512} \\\\ x+7 & =\\sqrt[9]{{2}^{9}} \\\\ x+7 & =2 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5ef8fbba-e17b-5d21-9b7e-67231bfee328"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ef8fbba-e17b-5d21-9b7e-67231bfee328" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef8fbba-e17b-5d21-9b7e-67231bfee328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c5610a42-df77-5563-8e3b-315f0bdd9b5c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81c72bf6-fc39-5e64-83f6-21c70539e4ee" "answer-c5610a42-df77-5563-8e3b-315f0bdd9b5c" "answer-4f8186ba-e3b0-5bd9-9843-2090471b6685" "answer-a70181af-098d-507c-9e5c-9a6c9cea4359" "answer-d50b88ab-07d6-5703-bc25-f4ee2a8d8d9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c72bf6-fc39-5e64-83f6-21c70539e4ee" :answer/id #uuid "81c72bf6-fc39-5e64-83f6-21c70539e4ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5610a42-df77-5563-8e3b-315f0bdd9b5c" :answer/id #uuid "c5610a42-df77-5563-8e3b-315f0bdd9b5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f8186ba-e3b0-5bd9-9843-2090471b6685" :answer/id #uuid "4f8186ba-e3b0-5bd9-9843-2090471b6685" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a70181af-098d-507c-9e5c-9a6c9cea4359" :answer/id #uuid "a70181af-098d-507c-9e5c-9a6c9cea4359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d50b88ab-07d6-5703-bc25-f4ee2a8d8d9e" :answer/id #uuid "d50b88ab-07d6-5703-bc25-f4ee2a8d8d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e173cb82-cae9-5da1-9ec4-a1b561689a6a" :question/id #uuid "e173cb82-cae9-5da1-9ec4-a1b561689a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-111453" :question/problem "Find the real solution to the equation $(x-5)^{3}=-27.$" :question/worked-solution "We can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$\nSince $n=3$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{3} & =-27 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(x-5)^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\ x-5 & =\\sqrt[3]{(-3)^{3}} \\\\ x-5 & =-3 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-580192e7-570b-5540-8797-e5c58d054e27"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-580192e7-570b-5540-8797-e5c58d054e27" :answer-field/id #uuid "580192e7-570b-5540-8797-e5c58d054e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-61d11fcf-2a35-5855-bdae-7f327a075eb6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad6b9e59-a711-5b03-a42f-7d2aaa7209c8" "answer-c4d00532-1734-576c-bad9-0b15fbfc48f4" "answer-6e6fd3ad-fa63-5890-9408-650907686585" "answer-61d11fcf-2a35-5855-bdae-7f327a075eb6" "answer-2b38477e-8cf2-57e3-940f-0e89aacc7ff2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad6b9e59-a711-5b03-a42f-7d2aaa7209c8" :answer/id #uuid "ad6b9e59-a711-5b03-a42f-7d2aaa7209c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4d00532-1734-576c-bad9-0b15fbfc48f4" :answer/id #uuid "c4d00532-1734-576c-bad9-0b15fbfc48f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e6fd3ad-fa63-5890-9408-650907686585" :answer/id #uuid "6e6fd3ad-fa63-5890-9408-650907686585" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61d11fcf-2a35-5855-bdae-7f327a075eb6" :answer/id #uuid "61d11fcf-2a35-5855-bdae-7f327a075eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b38477e-8cf2-57e3-940f-0e89aacc7ff2" :answer/id #uuid "2b38477e-8cf2-57e3-940f-0e89aacc7ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180684 :tutorial/content "How do we solve an equation with a variable raised to an odd exponent, such as\n\n$$\nx^3 = 125?\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by taking the $3$rd root of each side and solving for $x.$ \n\nSince $n=3$ is odd, there will be only one real solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =125 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}} & =\\sqrt[3]{125} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{{5}^{3}} \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5.$\n\nIn general, we have the following rule of thumb:\n\n*When $n$ is odd, and we take the $n$th root of both sides of $x^n = a,$ we get only one solution:* \n\n$$\nx = \\sqrt[n]{a}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179891 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186178624 :answer-field/choices 17592186178625] [:db/retract 17592186178624 :answer-field/choices 17592186178627] [:db/retract 17592186178624 :answer-field/choices 17592186178628] {:db/id 17592186179763 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-07885ed6-fd3c-5e89-9b4b-974d90f1b3c9" "question-b1e0dee6-7a44-5abb-b91d-4265ca1d15b0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179463 :question/problem "Simplify $9\\sqrt{p - 4} - 7\\sqrt{p - 4} .$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{p - 4}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\sqrt{p-4}-7\\sqrt{p-4} & = \\\\ (9-7)\\sqrt{p-4} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{p-4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179764 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bcc2a2a2-83b1-5938-a74c-5f79d37321a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179464 :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 3x}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-3\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (2-3)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ -\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179751 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70fd859a-d33f-544f-b045-d1ae93fdfb95" "question-a6334648-97e7-5622-8a2d-3ac7b05ed9c2" "question-09941e60-aba3-5a69-ab9a-c50e221cd8d0" "question-2b536617-f99c-5ac2-ab20-131751027d16"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179619 :question/problem "Simplify $10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ terms together, but we cannot combine the $\\sqrt[3]{y}$ and $\\sqrt{y}$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t10\\sqrt[3]{y} + 2\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(10 + 2)\\sqrt[3]{y} - 7\\sqrt{y} &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t12\\sqrt[3]{y}-7\\sqrt{y} &\n\t}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-07885ed6-fd3c-5e89-9b4b-974d90f1b3c9" :question/id #uuid "07885ed6-fd3c-5e89-9b4b-974d90f1b3c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-52394" :question/problem "$p\\sqrt{x}+q\\sqrt{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{x}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\sqrt{x}+q\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ p\\cdot \\sqrt{x}+q\\cdot \\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ (p+q)\\sqrt{x} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5999d2a9-f36a-5f69-8e3a-9981b335b405"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5999d2a9-f36a-5f69-8e3a-9981b335b405" :answer-field/id #uuid "5999d2a9-f36a-5f69-8e3a-9981b335b405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a596a05b-b96c-562c-ac17-a124fcdf385a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a596a05b-b96c-562c-ac17-a124fcdf385a" "answer-a45a06ff-3e53-5c5d-9d54-bac4613fd44b" "answer-25d10642-3f32-5349-83fc-e6491cc2d7d0" "answer-c24d2f73-41ea-580c-a26c-a3767f056a4d" "answer-cecc8a16-5543-50aa-aace-6409797f0f81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a596a05b-b96c-562c-ac17-a124fcdf385a" :answer/id #uuid "a596a05b-b96c-562c-ac17-a124fcdf385a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(p+q)\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a45a06ff-3e53-5c5d-9d54-bac4613fd44b" :answer/id #uuid "a45a06ff-3e53-5c5d-9d54-bac4613fd44b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(p+q)x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d10642-3f32-5349-83fc-e6491cc2d7d0" :answer/id #uuid "25d10642-3f32-5349-83fc-e6491cc2d7d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p+q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c24d2f73-41ea-580c-a26c-a3767f056a4d" :answer/id #uuid "c24d2f73-41ea-580c-a26c-a3767f056a4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "pq" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cecc8a16-5543-50aa-aace-6409797f0f81" :answer/id #uuid "cecc8a16-5543-50aa-aace-6409797f0f81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "pq\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b1e0dee6-7a44-5abb-b91d-4265ca1d15b0" :question/id #uuid "b1e0dee6-7a44-5abb-b91d-4265ca1d15b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-52395" :question/problem "$2p\\sqrt{y}-q\\sqrt{y}=$" :question/worked-solution "We can combine the two $\\sqrt{y}$ terms together, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p\\sqrt{y}-q\\sqrt{y} & = \\\\ 2p\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-q\\cdot \\sqrt{y} & = \\\\ (2p-q)\\sqrt{y} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dace7bbf-b422-5e70-b829-8a637b2e7746"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dace7bbf-b422-5e70-b829-8a637b2e7746" :answer-field/id #uuid "dace7bbf-b422-5e70-b829-8a637b2e7746" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4ff75db6-8ba4-526a-a519-335413e4ac2b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ff75db6-8ba4-526a-a519-335413e4ac2b" "answer-972a9aa4-598b-52a4-a773-a52358c681bc" "answer-a55d3d7e-4693-57f0-8376-bce5262512c1" "answer-cf4c7e42-ee11-55b0-81ae-d9b046e18ca5" "answer-c439e8e4-2e85-57ab-a5b2-71a06c2f0f0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ff75db6-8ba4-526a-a519-335413e4ac2b" :answer/id #uuid "4ff75db6-8ba4-526a-a519-335413e4ac2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2p-q)\\sqrt{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-972a9aa4-598b-52a4-a773-a52358c681bc" :answer/id #uuid "972a9aa4-598b-52a4-a773-a52358c681bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2p-q)y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a55d3d7e-4693-57f0-8376-bce5262512c1" :answer/id #uuid "a55d3d7e-4693-57f0-8376-bce5262512c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2pq\\sqrt{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf4c7e42-ee11-55b0-81ae-d9b046e18ca5" :answer/id #uuid "cf4c7e42-ee11-55b0-81ae-d9b046e18ca5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2p\\sqrt{y}}{q}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c439e8e4-2e85-57ab-a5b2-71a06c2f0f0e" :answer/id #uuid "c439e8e4-2e85-57ab-a5b2-71a06c2f0f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2p}{q\\sqrt{y}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180180 :question/problem "$2x\\sqrt{45}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x\\sqrt{45}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9\\cdot 5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 2x\\cdot 3\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 6x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ (6x-2x)\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x} & = \\\\ 4x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186178624 :answer-field/correct "answer-2aab4d00-4a59-532b-ae36-4832335d301e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8cd0a3f0-00f1-520b-9c34-359a3e5fdad5" "answer-2aab4d00-4a59-532b-ae36-4832335d301e" "answer-51a2289a-f9a9-5068-84bc-9c5f85953461"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8cd0a3f0-00f1-520b-9c34-359a3e5fdad5" :answer/id #uuid "8cd0a3f0-00f1-520b-9c34-359a3e5fdad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{45}+x\\sqrt{x}-2x\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2aab4d00-4a59-532b-ae36-4832335d301e" :answer/id #uuid "2aab4d00-4a59-532b-ae36-4832335d301e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51a2289a-f9a9-5068-84bc-9c5f85953461" :answer/id #uuid "51a2289a-f9a9-5068-84bc-9c5f85953461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x\\sqrt{5}+x\\sqrt{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bcc2a2a2-83b1-5938-a74c-5f79d37321a4" :question/id #uuid "bcc2a2a2-83b1-5938-a74c-5f79d37321a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-4062" :question/problem "$3\\sqrt{18b}+3\\sqrt{12b}+2\\sqrt{27b}=$" :question/worked-solution "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{18b}+3\\sqrt{12b}+2\\sqrt{27b} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{9\\cdot 2b}+3\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3b}+2\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3b} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{2b}+3\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3b}+2\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3b} & = \\\\ 3\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{2b}+3\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3b}+2\\cdot 3\\cdot \\sqrt{3b} & = \\\\ 9\\sqrt{2b}+6\\sqrt{3b}+6\\sqrt{3b} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9\\sqrt{2b}+6\\sqrt{3b}+6\\sqrt{3b} & = \\\\ 9\\sqrt{2b}+(6+6)\\sqrt{3b} & = \\\\ 9\\sqrt{2b}+12\\sqrt{3b} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f67f46d2-fe1c-5104-9d61-69319280e867"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f67f46d2-fe1c-5104-9d61-69319280e867" :answer-field/id #uuid "f67f46d2-fe1c-5104-9d61-69319280e867" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f5db809-d03e-58da-aed3-c6e305d1dda2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09b27bcd-d69a-57ab-86dc-d75b13132e84" "answer-e4655460-2e07-5417-ac02-40b55cc4b8d7" "answer-1f89ef35-2105-591f-b568-8c349c6c6c9a" "answer-9f5db809-d03e-58da-aed3-c6e305d1dda2" "answer-ac618e26-1e71-53d5-a4e7-3fc20e2dddd1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09b27bcd-d69a-57ab-86dc-d75b13132e84" :answer/id #uuid "09b27bcd-d69a-57ab-86dc-d75b13132e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\sqrt{5b}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4655460-2e07-5417-ac02-40b55cc4b8d7" :answer/id #uuid "e4655460-2e07-5417-ac02-40b55