we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({y}^{2}-\\frac{8}{3}y+2) & =-3({(y-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}+\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =-3{(y-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}+(-3)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =-3{(y-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5aa7cf4a-4ced-579f-b3b1-a8420309518b" "answer-field-6a7e8649-8e07-5c84-b1f7-d22b5da0ebf7" "answer-field-3d83943b-fa05-5a32-815b-4e9cc7e9a241"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5aa7cf4a-4ced-579f-b3b1-a8420309518b" :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa7cf4a-4ced-579f-b3b1-a8420309518b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2625b9b2-ccd2-5138-938a-0f951e89b71a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2625b9b2-ccd2-5138-938a-0f951e89b71a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2625b9b2-ccd2-5138-938a-0f951e89b71a" :answer/id #uuid "2625b9b2-ccd2-5138-938a-0f951e89b71a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6a7e8649-8e07-5c84-b1f7-d22b5da0ebf7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a7e8649-8e07-5c84-b1f7-d22b5da0ebf7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-108be57e-a123-56a8-8b6d-ef26347eebd9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-108be57e-a123-56a8-8b6d-ef26347eebd9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-108be57e-a123-56a8-8b6d-ef26347eebd9" :answer/id #uuid "108be57e-a123-56a8-8b6d-ef26347eebd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d83943b-fa05-5a32-815b-4e9cc7e9a241" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d83943b-fa05-5a32-815b-4e9cc7e9a241" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e8dcca78-6127-52c8-a7fd-0263cd403f9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8dcca78-6127-52c8-a7fd-0263cd403f9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8dcca78-6127-52c8-a7fd-0263cd403f9b" :answer/id #uuid "e8dcca78-6127-52c8-a7fd-0263cd403f9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fc2b2629-e323-5ab5-9be3-1b12132dec56" :question/id #uuid "fc2b2629-e323-5ab5-9be3-1b12132dec56" :question/math-academy-id "q-140379" :question/problem "Rewrite $-8{x}^{2}-4x$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-8.$ So, we take out a factor of $-8$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-8({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}x+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{16}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x) & =-8({(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-8{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =-8{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6e4a4bf-3e09-5621-be81-4a8b258251af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6e4a4bf-3e09-5621-be81-4a8b258251af" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6e4a4bf-3e09-5621-be81-4a8b258251af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb62be8e-3070-5be6-b38d-3a062278e1f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b17792ba-6da9-5712-933a-ecb6ba3164b4" "answer-260cd36f-3cd1-5e6e-a08e-7d3ca9370c8c" "answer-aea1e521-d9dc-5058-a940-b2513a2a3010" "answer-cb62be8e-3070-5be6-b38d-3a062278e1f0" "answer-7ba08eda-a7a0-539e-92cd-414b03d79077"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b17792ba-6da9-5712-933a-ecb6ba3164b4" :answer/id #uuid "b17792ba-6da9-5712-933a-ecb6ba3164b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-260cd36f-3cd1-5e6e-a08e-7d3ca9370c8c" :answer/id #uuid "260cd36f-3cd1-5e6e-a08e-7d3ca9370c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aea1e521-d9dc-5058-a940-b2513a2a3010" :answer/id #uuid "aea1e521-d9dc-5058-a940-b2513a2a3010" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb62be8e-3070-5be6-b38d-3a062278e1f0" :answer/id #uuid "cb62be8e-3070-5be6-b38d-3a062278e1f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ba08eda-a7a0-539e-92cd-414b03d79077" :answer/id #uuid "7ba08eda-a7a0-539e-92cd-414b03d79077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-517afe53-217c-5ede-9811-b9bf164398f6" :question/id #uuid "517afe53-217c-5ede-9811-b9bf164398f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-140380" :question/problem "Rewrite $-5{y}^{2}+2y+\\frac{4}{5}$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-5.$ So, we take out a factor of $-5$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-5({y}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}y-\\frac{4}{25})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}y-\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}y-\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{4}{25}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}y+{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({y}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}y-\\frac{4}{25}) & =-5({(y-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =-5{(y-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}+(-5)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =-5{(y-\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28822793-1aa6-5555-91d5-42b23da22347"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28822793-1aa6-5555-91d5-42b23da22347" :answer-field/id #uuid "28822793-1aa6-5555-91d5-42b23da22347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d96310d9-2183-516b-b152-b846ac135e7d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7cc5889c-f956-5805-828b-a07b04225e9d" "answer-f499ebac-94ab-572a-a984-e07f21d31ab5" "answer-d96310d9-2183-516b-b152-b846ac135e7d" "answer-805a1efe-9356-5170-a269-8ed6c903aa17" "answer-d93ffed7-ac55-5ecb-a0d9-3189b1b4cd84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7cc5889c-f956-5805-828b-a07b04225e9d" :answer/id #uuid "7cc5889c-f956-5805-828b-a07b04225e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{(y+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f499ebac-94ab-572a-a984-e07f21d31ab5" :answer/id #uuid "f499ebac-94ab-572a-a984-e07f21d31ab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5{(y+\\frac{1}{5})}^{2}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d96310d9-2183-516b-b152-b846ac135e